==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[groovey]]

===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-uːvi|-uːvi]]

===Etymology 1===
See [[groove]].

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|groovi|er}}

# Of, pertaining to, or having [[grooves]].
#:''The back of the tile was '''groovy''' so that it could hold the adhesive compound.''

===Etymology 2===
From the phrase ''[[in the groove]]'', ultimately from the grooves of an early phonograph record.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|groovi|er}}

# {{context|dated|slang}} [[cool|Cool]], [[neat]], [[interesting]].
#:''Wow, man!  This psychedelic screen saver is totally '''groovy'''!'' ^^ so l33t

